claim.claim-text:
identifying (2105) a traffic periodicity associated with wireless communications traffic to a user equipment, UE;
determining (2110), based at least in part on the traffic periodicity, a plurality of discontinuous reception cycles arranged to be spaced within a discontinuous reception period, the plurality of discontinuous reception cycles having a plurality of ON-durations during which the UE is to wake up from a sleep mode to monitor for the wireless communications traffic, and at least one start time for an additional ON-duration different from the ON-duration of the discontinuous reception cycle, the start time for the additional ON-duration being within the discontinuous reception period; and
transmitting (2115) a discontinuous reception cycle configuration that indicates at least the discontinuous reception cycle associated with the discontinuous reception period to the UE, wherein the transmitting comprises transmitting an indication of a non-integer rational number, the non-integer rational number being associated with the start time for the additional ON-duration.

identify (2105) a traffic periodicity associated with wireless communications traffic to a user equipment, UE;
determine (2110), based at least in part on the traffic periodicity, a plurality of discontinuous reception cycles arranged to be spaced within a discontinuous reception period, the plurality of discontinuous reception cycles having a plurality of ON-durations during which the LTE is to wake up from a sleep mode to monitor for the wireless communications traffic, and at least one start time for an additional ON-duration different from the ON-duration of the discontinuous reception cycle, the start time for the additional ON-duration being within the discontinuous reception period; and
transmit (2115) a discontinuous reception cycle configuration that indicates at least the discontinuous reception cycle associated with the discontinuous reception period to the UE, wherein the transmitting comprises transmitting an indication of a non-integer rational number, the non-integer rational number being associated with the start time for the additional ON-duration.
